'''Work in progress.''' This is an unofficial downstream port on the vendor
4.19 kernel. Display, touchscreen, speaker audio, '''Wi-Fi''' and
'''Bluetooth''' work, and the device boots into Phosh, associates to a network
and brings its Bluetooth controller up on its own.

Not working: modem, cameras, brightness control and GPU acceleration (the
compositor runs on the pixman software renderer). The battery charges and, since kernel
r26, the fuel gauge reports a level. SSH works over Wi-Fi but stalls over the
USB link (see [[#Known issues]]).

Connectivity is the notable part: MT6833 has no mainline support for it, so
this port reconstructs MediaTek's gen4m stack for the SoC and replaces the
Android launcher daemon with small userspace services. Bluetooth shares the
same chip; its vendor driver only exposes a character device for Android's
stack, so a small bridge presents it to BlueZ through the kernel's virtual HCI
transport. Bluetooth audio negotiates but does not play — the device has no
audio session to consume it. Do not expect a daily driver.

